 #:seon.task{:name "register-works-only-top-level"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.schema/register!` inside let or any nested form refuses 'Schema declarations require an isolated registration delta' (schema.clj:1279): the delta opens only for a syntactically top-level register!. The first run of three register! took 1,786 ms and eight took 3,681 ms. Open the delta around any register! reached during a form."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/begin-registration-delta seon.schema/register!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/schema-registration-works-only-as-a-top-level-form.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-projection-travels-ambiently"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The projection still travels in dynamic Vars (*projection*, *projection-state*, *packaged-forms*, *candidate-forms-overlay*) plus a registration-delta candidate atom: 18 handed-projection, 42 call-with-projection (16 files), 12 call-with-projection-state and 5 call-with-forms call sites. `seon.db/carried-projection` already answers the same value in 0.01 ms. The current JVM's profile shows call-with-projection-state inclusive 229,243 ms, max 55,673 ms, x97, which also hides real costs from profiles. Convert readers to the carried projection and delete the ambient Vars (C5); C2 waits on this."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.schema/call-with-projection seon.schema/call-with-projection-state seon.schema/handed-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/delete-r8-r6-r10-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "map-validation-throws-on-sorted-maps-with-foreign-keys"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Malli's :map validator looks each declared key up (malli core.cljc:1276); a sorted map whose comparator cannot compare that key with its own keys throws ClassCastException instead of answering false (fault fa60ad84, `seon.schema/valid-candidate-value?` from turn-step, 17:13Z). The producer site was fixed in `seon.turn/disposition` (f83931226) by validating only maps that name the discriminator, and `seon.render.value/keyword-lookup?` guards the same class in render: two copies of one guard. Validating an arbitrary value against a candidate schema belongs to one owner; decide there, once, so callers delete their guards. At the agent REPL the throw escaped settlement and wedged the run; a throw while validating must settle as that form's failure."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/valid-candidate-value? seon.turn/disposition seon.render.value/keyword-lookup?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-boot-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/armed-error-validation-throws-on-non-keyword-sorted-maps.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-function-contract-changes-the-schema-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Function contract entities are a projection range (`seon.schema/projection-ranges` :function-contract-rows), so every contracted defn makes a new projection value: load-projection (36-50 ms, ~94 MB) and every projection-keyed derivation re-walks ~3,550 forms. Measured 2026-09-26 on pid 89341: (defn f [x] (inc x)) 134 ms, 157 MB, 26k armed calls; the same defn with {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} 757 ms, 1.21 GB, 190k armed calls. Root ruling 2026-09-27: contracts leave the projection; design in docs/research/agent-platform/contracts-out-of-projection-design-2026-09-27.md."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/projection-ranges seon.schema/build-projection seon.db/carried-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/defn-scan-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/contracts-out-of-projection-design-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "pull-selector-predicate-compiles-per-check"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.schema/pull-selector?` compiles its whole argument (Datahike compile-pull-plan) on every armed `:seon.schema/pull-selector` check: 0.69 ms for the 15,060-node root selector, ten checks per walk since 18ce1b1a4 armed vector-pull and physical-selector (sci.eval-test public-walk counted 10 compiles for one plan, E6). projection-with-pulled-form-in's hit costs 2.9-3.1 ms digesting its key. Parse once per selector value (a content-keyed cache kind) or check structure only."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/pull-selector? seon.schema/projection-with-pulled-form-in}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-r6-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "schema-registration-rechecks-the-whole-program-per-key"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Historical registration samples re-derived every contract's references at about 300 ms per key. H10 retains contract products in the projection. Candidate e6d124cbbac923824ce1063f58bff689b1805e5f, run f960d3eb3561: one register! staged through begin-registration-delta costs 20.08 ms, 19.260272 MB and 3,727 armed calls, with one contract-references walk for the new declaration, rather than a walk per contract. The pre-change live SCI probe on sol-h10-references cost 8 ms and 15.4 MB for the value, but 468.1 ms and 120,196 calls for its whole request (result/efe03f45bac17); these are different scopes, not a speedup claim. Measure the complete registration request on the installed H10 program and attribute its remaining work; done when its cost follows the registered declarations and affected contracts and the full request is under 100 ms."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register! seon.schema/begin-registration-delta seon.schema/contract-product seon.schema/contract-references seon.instrument-test/a-cold-base-reads-retained-contract-references}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/health-recording-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-check-on-three-files-exceeds-one-second",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "Review static check of seon.print, seon.render.value and value-test against packaged resources at 0daf87818 took 1301.291 ms after external JVM replacement; earlier same-class checks took 168.540 and 222.844 ms. Measure which installed contract-check operations repeat and preserve correctness; no causal ranking yet. Required full-tree clj-kondo --cache false on the archive also took 10739 ms over 494 files (0 errors/1488 warnings); that run is explicitly requested review work proportional to the whole tree, not an ordinary print. Record gate acquisition separately from warm execution; do not turn a timing observation into a wall-clock regression test.",
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-codex-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-registration-refusal-carries-an-error-type"
  :kind :function
  :intent "register! of [:maybe :int] returns a flat map with layer and member but no `:seon.error/type` (registration-refusal, schema.clj:1643). Every error is one flat map with `:seon.error/type` extending `:seon.error/base`, built by the installed constructor `seon.error.refusal/error`. Proof: schema-design.md probe 3 answers a map whose `:seon.error/type` is a registered variant."
  :must-read #{seon.schema/registration-refusal}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/schema-design.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "schema-only-derivations-are-rederived-per-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "projection-cache-value holds each derivation by the projection value, and every contracted defn builds a new projection, so every derivation that reads only schema forms is recomputed after each definition: on default the pass after a defn spends 25-37 MB re-deriving program-attributes (fixed by holding it by forms and admissions), observation-selector (12.8 MB), declared-schema-keys (1.6 MB), shapes-in (2.1 MB) and the storable-attribute plans; that pass costs 94-97 MB and 57,000 armed calls against 55 MB and 8,000 for an ordinary pass (defn-why, 2026-10-08). Give the projection a schema-population identity that a contract-only write keeps (the advanced projection knows no schema row changed) and hold schema-only derivations by it. Done when the pass after a contract-only defn costs what an ordinary pass costs."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/projection-cache-value seon.schema/load-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/defn-why/defn-why.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-durable-projection-cache-evicts-a-commits-entry-across-tests-sharing-a-jvm"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.schema.projection-writer-test/a-new-branch-at-an-equal-commit-reads-the-held-projection` passes alone and with its own namespace but fails (one `seon.db/declaration-content-key` call) when run in one JVM with `seon.db-test` and `seon.schema-test` tests, at HEAD and with PB-08 (2026-10-09): the likely cause is the 24-entry durable projection cache (`seon.db/carried-projection`, `content-projection`) evicting the commit's entry. Either the bound is a dial sized from what projections weigh, or the test owns its cache state."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-contract-naming-an-unregistered-schema-is-refused-as-a-platform-fault"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent's `(defn expected-form {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :malli.core/schema] :any]} [schema] ...)` in seon.error (fan-out 6, agent fan6-enum, default 6e9b9017c) is refused as `seon.schema/canonical-definition` breaking its own output contract (`:seon.instrument/contract-error`, 'expected :seon.schema/malli-form ..., got a vector. Fix: Change seon/schema.clj:646.'), a fix the agent cannot act on, instead of naming `:malli.core/schema` as a schema the registry does not hold. The reply carries the whole diagnostic map (about 750 tokens: two digests, caller twice, layer, `:at`, the message again inside its problem). Done when such a defn is refused as the agent's error naming the unregistered key and how to register or replace it, asserted on the reply's data."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/canonical-definition seon.fn/var-entity}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-function-arities-in"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Give `seon.schema/function-arities-in` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it (`docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`): registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, file a task on the producer naming `seon.schema/function-arities-in` in its must-read with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/function-arities-in seon.contracts/gaps}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-contract-naming-an-unresolvable-symbol-refuses-the-whole-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A function contract that is a valid Malli form but names a qualified symbol that resolves to no schema or predicate refuses the whole projection: `seon.schema/projection-registry` compiles every function symbol in one `doseq` and turns the first failure into `seon.schema/refuse-unresolved-reference!`, so `seon.schema/build-projection` throws `:malli.core/invalid-schema` for the population. Reproduced at default's JVM REPL (lane publication-robust, 2026-10-10): `(seon.schema/build-projection (:seon.schema.projection/forms p) (assoc (:seon.schema.projection/function-contracts p) 'x.y/f '[:=> [:cat seon.dev.docstring/format-findings-request-schema] :string]) (assoc (seon.schema/population-options p) :seon.schema/projection p))` with `p` the carried projection of default's database. The same contract passes `seon.schema/malli-form?` and `seon.schema/canonical-definition`, so the indexer's `:seon.fn/malformed-spec` translation (`seon.fn/authored-contract`) does not catch it. Done when such a contract is kept as data and unarmed, listed as a problem on its function, and every other declaration still compiles."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/projection-registry seon.schema/build-projection seon.schema/canonical-definition seon.fn/authored-contract}}
 #:seon.task{:name "registering-a-schema-refuses-a-redefined-core-contract-the-defn-admitted"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On one branch, `(defn seon.render.web/stop! ...)` with its shipped contract unchanged (`[:=> [:cat :seon.render.web/stop-request] [:or :nil :seon.await/timeout-error]]`) is admitted, and then `(seon.schema/register! :seon.render.web/server '[:map ... [:seon.render.web/executor :seon.flow/executor]])` answers `:seon.schema/nilable-return` for `seon.render.web/stop!` (lane chain-4's branch, 2026-10-12); registering the same form first and redefining `stop!` second admits both. In the same eval request the refusal un-settles every form (`Not settled: this run's settlement was refused`). Two admission paths judge one contract differently: `seon.schema/register!` re-walks the referencing contract as agent-authored (`seon.schema.internal` nilable-union rule), while the defn kept it. Chain experiment 4 met it in attempts 3 and 4. Correct: one admission decision per contract, the same on both paths. No proof yet: a test through `stop!` runs its 48 reaching web tests in the test step; the proof wants a smaller shipped function with a nilable return whose input schema is registrable."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register! seon.schema/projection-with-function-contract}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-4.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fn-schema-over-a-branch-predicate-is-refused"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent that defines a predicate on its branch cannot name it in a schema: after `(defn seon.render.web/c4-probe-executor? ...)` on a branch, `(seon.schema/malli-form? '[:fn seon.render.web/c4-probe-executor?])` answers false and `(seon.schema/register! k '[:fn ns/pred?])` refuses `:seon.schema/definition` (\"got a vector\"), while `'[:fn seon.render.web/server?]`, a compiled Var, answers true. `seon.schema/malli-form?` resolves `:fn` predicate symbols against host Vars, not the evaluation's SCI context, so the shipped `[:fn {...} ns/pred?]` shape is out of an agent's reach. Chain experiment 4 met it in attempts 1 and 2 (five refusals). Correct: a schema form names a predicate the registering world defines."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/malli-form? seon.schema/register!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-4.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-schema-naming-a-branch-predicate-breaks-the-test-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On a branch, `(defn ok? ...)` then `(seon.schema/register! :n/thing '[:map [:n/x n/ok?]])` is admitted (the bare symbol resolves as the branch's program predicate). From then on the declared reads of that branch's test step refuse `:malli.core/invalid-schema` naming `n/ok?` from `seon.schema/direct-reference-keys-in` (reached through `seon.db/carried-projection` from `seon.test/definition-digests`), on every later eval request, while reads of the branch head itself answer: a projection built for another value of the branch lacks the branch's predicates. Chain experiment 4 (J1): attempt `ee6cfaeb5c0b` sat 4 min with no end; default's recorded error 7c40461fc9f6 when root's stop read that branch's open turn; reproduced at HEAD 7ef4967db on lane faults-rc's branch (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/db-clean/root-causes.md`). One admission decision: either every projection of the branch resolves its predicates as `seon.schema/register!` did, or `register!` refuses a bare function symbol. No proof yet: through `seon.test-support/with-running-agent`, the same register! followed by an agent defn and deftest leaves the test step green (lane faults-rc, `bin/seon check`), so the refusing projection is the one built for the reaching platform tests' world (`seon.test/clean-request-handle`) on that branch; the proof must reach a platform test from the branch. Done when the test step of such a branch reads it."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register! seon.schema/direct-reference-keys-in seon.db/carried-projection seon.test/definition-digests}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-4.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/db-clean/root-causes.md"}}]
